WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.070 --> 00:00:05.029
Hey youtubers it’s Charlie and this is going
to be my Flash Episode 7 video.

00:00:05.029 --> 00:00:07.980
There were a ton of great easter eggs and
the Barry Allen character turned another giant

00:00:07.980 --> 00:00:17.310
corner in terms of 
his development.

00:00:17.310 --> 00:00:22.009
Lots of great Harrison Wells moments that
both answered and raised more questions.

00:00:22.009 --> 00:00:25.230
My position on who he is didn’t change much
but we can examine the evidence.

00:00:25.230 --> 00:00:27.990
Careful for spoilers in case you haven’t
seen the episode.

00:00:27.990 --> 00:00:29.169
Starting with TOP 5 moments.

00:00:29.169 --> 00:00:31.099
Number 5 - Meet Farooq aka Blackout

00:00:31.099 --> 00:00:37.280
He’s another casualty of STAR Labs but he’s
one of the first to demonize Harrison Wells

00:00:37.280 --> 00:00:38.989
in the eyes of Team Flash.

00:00:38.989 --> 00:00:42.010
I think being scientists, Caitlin and Cisco
are a little more flexible on the matter.

00:00:42.010 --> 00:00:44.199
Doing what is necessary versus doing what
is right.

00:00:44.199 --> 00:00:48.149
Barry has the same alignment as Superman,
which makes him a total boy scout.

00:00:48.149 --> 00:00:53.769
So Farooq isn’t a villain.

00:00:53.769 --> 00:00:57.519
In the comics he did work with the Rogues.

00:00:57.519 --> 00:01:00.390
We mostly see him during the Flashpoint storyline.

00:01:00.390 --> 00:01:04.400
Which is really cool because Barry getting
his powers back in the episode looked like

00:01:04.400 --> 00:01:06.000
a scene from that same comic.

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:12.460
In the context of the story he’s the most
powerful source of electricity on earth.

00:01:12.460 --> 00:01:15.830
Or you could think of him as the world’s
most powerful conductor.

00:01:15.830 --> 00:01:18.229
Which is why Harrison Wells wants to study
him.

00:01:18.229 --> 00:01:20.750
He’s one of the few things The Flash is
vulnerable to.

00:01:20.750 --> 00:01:28.830
And going with the canon of the show, he only
steals the energy of the speed force, as if

00:01:28.830 --> 00:01:33.799
Barry Allen’s cells stored energy the same
way Superman’s cells store solar radiation

00:01:33.799 --> 00:01:35.829
and that’s what gives them both their abilities.

00:01:35.829 --> 00:01:37.450
Don’t worry about the specifics.

00:01:37.450 --> 00:01:41.310
The show is always really good about explaining
the science behind what they do, so when Harrison

00:01:41.310 --> 00:01:44.979
Wells starts messing with Farooq’s DNA we’ll
get details.

00:01:44.979 --> 00:01:56.990
For Now, Farooq is going to chill in 

00:01:56.990 --> 00:02:01.120
the meta prison.

00:02:01.120 --> 00:02:05.049
Number 4 - Barry Allen is jacking around too
much

00:02:05.049 --> 00:02:10.250
The Flash as a character takes himself much
less seriously than say Batman, Superman,

00:02:10.250 --> 00:02:11.250
even Green Arrow.

00:02:11.250 --> 00:02:14.671
He’s a lot more like Hal Jordan, which is
why they usually only break through barriers

00:02:14.671 --> 00:02:18.530
both mental and physical, after getting their
asses handed to them.

00:02:18.530 --> 00:02:22.861
They’re not super zen characters, so Barry
getting his butt kicked all the time is a

00:02:22.861 --> 00:02:26.500
very necessary part of the process of unlocking
his potential.

00:02:26.500 --> 00:02:32.021
Harrison Wells reaction was way more subdued
than I thought it would be, we kind of saw

00:02:32.021 --> 00:02:34.910
the real Harrison slip out when their lives
were all on the line.

00:02:34.910 --> 00:02:39.110
We’ve seen him lose it in front of Cisco
back when he learned about the Cold Gun.

00:02:39.110 --> 00:02:42.370
All his energy is bent on getting Barry to
a hundred percent.

00:02:42.370 --> 00:02:46.730
That’s the stratosphere of power where Barry
can phase through solid objects, break into

00:02:46.730 --> 00:02:49.250
other dimensions and travel through time.

00:02:49.250 --> 00:02:52.870
Like he said, More Speed is the Key.

00:02:52.870 --> 00:02:58.780
Number 3 - The Clock King is Back

00:02:58.780 --> 00:03:02.150
It may have just been me, but it seemed like
Robert Knepper’s performance was decidedly

00:03:02.150 --> 00:03:04.810
more comic booky than when he was on Arrow.

00:03:04.810 --> 00:03:07.120
It almost sounded like he developed a whole
new accent.

00:03:07.120 --> 00:03:11.920
One that sounded a lot more like the Clock
King from the Animated Series.

00:03:11.920 --> 00:03:14.240
He also spoke a lot more lines out of the
comics.

00:03:14.240 --> 00:03:17.810
For instance, anytime he did wordplay with
time and clocks, those lines were right out

00:03:17.810 --> 00:03:18.810
of the comics.

00:03:18.810 --> 00:03:21.580
Like when he said “Time and Time wait for
no man”.

00:03:21.580 --> 00:03:25.790
I loved his performance but the police station
scenes felt a little uneven with the Star

00:03:25.790 --> 00:03:26.830
Labs scenes.

00:03:26.830 --> 00:03:31.650
I’m still not super connected to the Iris
character yet, so when she was kidnapped it

00:03:31.650 --> 00:03:36.730
just didn’t quite feel like Arrow when the
old Count Vertigo threatened to inject Felicity.

00:03:36.730 --> 00:03:40.100
To be fair that was Arrow Season 2 and The
Flash hasn’t even finished half of it’s

00:03:40.100 --> 00:03:41.100
first season yet.

00:03:41.100 --> 00:03:44.391
So I’ll give Candice Patton and the writers
the benefit of the doubt.

00:03:44.391 --> 00:03:47.760
It’s really hard for all the other women
on Arrow and The Flash to hold screen time

00:03:47.760 --> 00:03:48.760
with Felicity.

00:03:48.760 --> 00:03:53.730
That just means that anytime any other women
are on screen with Felicity, you’re attention

00:03:53.730 --> 00:03:55.620
will typically be drawn to her.

00:03:55.620 --> 00:04:04.260
You’re always going to be drawn to the strongest
character on screen when there are a bunch

00:04:04.260 --> 00:04:24.800
of people in 
focus at the same time.

00:04:24.800 --> 00:04:31.930
I really did love Iris’ line when she said
“sometimes a girl has to save herself”.

00:04:31.930 --> 00:04:35.860
That’s very telling for where all the ArrowVerse
females this year.

00:04:35.860 --> 00:04:38.180
They’re all seriously stepping up their
game.

00:04:38.180 --> 00:04:42.280
Powers or no Powers.

00:04:42.280 --> 00:04:45.790
Number 2 - Barry Gets His Powers Back and
Then Some

00:04:45.790 --> 00:04:49.930
Using an electric charge to get his powers
back was a very similar thing to what happened

00:04:49.930 --> 00:04:51.560
in Flashpoint Paradox.

00:04:51.560 --> 00:04:55.530
In the comic he had to completely re-create
the accident that gave him powers the first

00:04:55.530 --> 00:04:56.530
time.

00:04:56.530 --> 00:05:03.290
There were all the chemicals and they had
to use a bolt of electricity.

00:05:03.290 --> 00:05:07.080
On the show they used the Treadmill because
Cisco had jacked it’s power way way up.

00:05:07.080 --> 00:05:09.550
That’s why it’s able to go so fast when
Barry Runs on it.

00:05:09.550 --> 00:05:13.410
It has like megawatts of electricity going
through it.

00:05:13.410 --> 00:05:15.890
When he said it didn’t work it was also
a reference to Flashpoint.

00:05:15.890 --> 00:05:19.750
In the comic Barry had to get struck by a
bolt of lightning twice, the first time it

00:05:19.750 --> 00:05:22.130
just burnt him like crispy chicken.

00:05:22.130 --> 00:05:34.610
The second time it worked and he was able
to heal himself almost instantly.

00:05:34.610 --> 00:05:44.130
Flashpoint in general was a 
big time travel story, so it’s no coincidence

00:05:44.130 --> 00:05:47.690
that the show is pushing into more time travel.

00:05:47.690 --> 00:05:56.730
Mostly via Harrison Wells computer Gideon.

00:05:56.730 --> 00:06:29.139
Now that Barry has broken through a big mental
barrier we might see him phase through something

00:06:29.139 --> 00:06:33.620
in the back half of the season.

00:06:33.620 --> 00:06:38.290
There’s still a lot of stuff he has to learn
to do before that and he still has to have

00:06:38.290 --> 00:06:42.370
his Empire Strikes Back moment where he confronts
the Reverse Flash and gets his ass handed

00:06:42.370 --> 00:06:57.590
to 

00:06:57.590 --> 00:07:01.060
him big time.

00:07:01.060 --> 00:07:08.460
The producers were talking about that recently
so after my top 5 moments I’ll explain what

00:07:08.460 --> 00:07:09.460
they said.

00:07:09.460 --> 00:07:13.110
My Number 1 moment was of course Harrison
Wells plan unfolding more in front of our

00:07:13.110 --> 00:07:14.110
eyes

00:07:14.110 --> 00:07:16.830
Lots of questions answered, but I didn’t
feel like they significantly answered yes

00:07:16.830 --> 00:07:20.810
or no, who is he really?

00:07:20.810 --> 00:07:24.030
Let’s start with the language he used when
he was talking to his computer.

00:07:24.030 --> 00:07:26.169
“The future is still intact”.

00:07:26.169 --> 00:07:31.220
Then he said to Cisco “Of all my inventions,
The Flash is the most important”.

00:07:31.220 --> 00:07:35.440
Right off the bat I think we have a modified
Flashpoint Paradox storyline going on here.

00:07:35.440 --> 00:07:38.970
Originally the producers said they’d be
sticking really close to the Flash Rebirth

00:07:38.970 --> 00:07:39.970
storyline.

00:07:39.970 --> 00:07:41.630
Which is a totally different series of events.

00:07:41.630 --> 00:07:44.130
Now I think it’s a combination of both comics.

00:07:44.130 --> 00:07:47.590
Rebirth is the story of Barry Allen’s origin
story.

00:07:47.590 --> 00:07:51.760
Flashpoint Paradox is the story of what happens
when Barry and The Reverse Flash mess with

00:07:51.760 --> 00:07:52.760
the timeline.

00:07:52.760 --> 00:07:57.200
They’re both responsible for messing things
up, but Barry is the one who has to fix it.

00:07:57.200 --> 00:08:02.610
Right now it seems like Harrison Wells is
the self-appointed protector of the timeline.

00:08:02.610 --> 00:08:06.160
He has a futuristic computer, so I still think
he’s either working with someone from the

00:08:06.160 --> 00:08:10.560
future like the Reverse Flash or he is the
Reverse Flash in the future and the version

00:08:10.560 --> 00:08:23.669
of him we’re seeing is stuck in the past
without powers.

00:08:23.669 --> 00:08:27.780
Time Loops can get confusing, so I’ll give
mad props to the writers on Flash for explaining

00:08:27.780 --> 00:08:32.500
the Paradox in a really relatable way.

00:08:32.500 --> 00:08:39.690
I highly recommend you read Flashpoint Paradox
or watch the animated movie if you’ve never

00:08:39.690 --> 00:08:40.690
seen it.

00:08:40.690 --> 00:08:43.260
It’s another Geoff Johns story.

00:08:43.260 --> 00:08:47.570
Just the fact Wells named his computer AI
Gideon says a lot too.

00:08:47.570 --> 00:08:50.360
Gideon was a Judge of the Isrealites in the
Hebrew Bible.

00:08:50.360 --> 00:08:52.770
His story is part of the Book of Judges.

00:08:52.770 --> 00:08:56.190
Gideon is also considered a Saint in the Catholic
Church.

00:08:56.190 --> 00:09:02.270
This is an oversimplification but he’s chosen
by God to get the Israelites to believe in

00:09:02.270 --> 00:09:06.070
the one true god and turn away from false
idols.

00:09:06.070 --> 00:09:09.940
He succeeds, but then after his death everyone
starts worshipping another god again.

00:09:09.940 --> 00:09:14.820
In Flashpoint, the Geoff Johns comic, there’s
a character named Libra who’s name in latin

00:09:14.820 --> 00:09:15.820
means “weighing scales”.

00:09:15.820 --> 00:09:20.140
The symbol implies balance.

00:09:20.140 --> 00:09:22.720
Harrison Wells has a lot of those ideas in
his character.

00:09:22.720 --> 00:09:27.110
He’s not overtly good or bad, he’s trying
to balance the future.

00:09:27.110 --> 00:09:29.590
That doesn’t mean that he’s the Libra
character from the comics, that character

00:09:29.590 --> 00:09:30.940
secretly turned out to be someone else in
disguise.

00:09:30.940 --> 00:09:32.760
So here’s my big question for you guys.

00:09:32.760 --> 00:09:36.480
Do you think he’s the Libra character or
do you still think he’s Professor Zoom?

00:09:36.480 --> 00:09:40.810
Remember, he’s going to develop a method
for stealing the Flash’s powers.

00:09:40.810 --> 00:09:46.180
But he could also use that to steal the Reverse
Flash’s powers too.

00:09:46.180 --> 00:09:50.260
So not evil but not good either.

00:09:50.260 --> 00:09:53.870
The biggest easter eggs I saw outside of Libra
and the Flashpoint stuff were the names Harrison

00:09:53.870 --> 00:09:54.870
rattles off.

00:09:54.870 --> 00:09:56.690
They’re all lesser comic book characters.

00:09:56.690 --> 00:09:59.730
He named Ralph Dinby, Elongated Man.

00:09:59.730 --> 00:10:07.070
Will Everett, Amazing Man, Al Rothstein, Atom-Smasher
from JSA, Bea Da Costa, who was a hero named

00:10:07.070 --> 00:10:12.910
fire, Grant Emerson aka Damage and of course
Ronnie Raymond, who we know is going to come

00:10:12.910 --> 00:10:14.670
back in a couple episodes as Firestorm.

00:10:14.670 --> 00:10:18.380
If you spotted any other easter eggs in the
video that I didn’t mention just write them

00:10:18.380 --> 00:10:20.070
in the comments.

00:10:20.070 --> 00:10:25.650
Overall I gave the episode a B plus, amazing
Flash story at Star Labs with an uneven Police

00:10:25.650 --> 00:10:27.010
Story with Clock King.

00:10:27.010 --> 00:10:33.600
I’m not really sure if the episode even
needed Clock King, although Robert Knepper

00:10:33.600 --> 00:10:35.350
was amazing as always.

00:10:35.350 --> 00:10:38.670
Always more prison break actors.

00:10:38.670 --> 00:10:47.430
I love that the show has snagged so many of
them.

00:10:47.430 --> 00:10:51.240
Tom Cavanagh once again, the most interesting
character in the episode.

00:10:51.240 --> 00:10:56.870
I’m starting to understand why he chose
this role.

00:10:56.870 --> 00:11:00.310
Arguably he’s big enough to headline his
own series.

00:11:00.310 --> 00:11:05.870
Usually when a bigger actor signs on for a
part like this it’s because secretly the

00:11:05.870 --> 00:11:14.860
lesser character they’re playing becomes
way way more important later in the series.

00:11:14.860 --> 00:11:20.110
I’m totally feeling the Caitlin, Cisco,
Barry Team Flash jam that’s going on.

00:11:20.110 --> 00:11:22.839
They all work so well together they feel like
family at this point.

00:11:22.839 --> 00:11:24.010
Just like Team Arrow.

00:11:24.010 --> 00:11:27.690
And that’s the reason why I think both of
these shows are so much better than all the

00:11:27.690 --> 00:11:33.200
other comic book shows.

00:11:33.200 --> 00:11:40.480
They focus on the characters and not so much
the spectacle of superpowers.

00:11:40.480 --> 00:11:45.840
Joss Whedon had this rule about writing that
said ‘fall in love with moments’ as in

00:11:45.840 --> 00:11:50.100
moments between characters ‘don’t fall
in love with moves” moves being the big

00:11:50.100 --> 00:11:53.730
reveal of Harrison Wells having a secret future
computer.

00:11:53.730 --> 00:11:58.370
That means nothing if Barry and Team Flash
hasn’t gone through some journey together

00:11:58.370 --> 00:12:01.310
that ties directly to the Harrison Reveal.

00:12:01.310 --> 00:12:06.540
Team Flash is like a family right now, so
when Barry Learns what Harrison is really

00:12:06.540 --> 00:12:10.550
doing, it will have this big resounding impact
and we the audience will all be like “holy

00:12:10.550 --> 00:12:11.550
shit”

00:12:11.550 --> 00:12:16.040
Greg Berlanti, Andrew Kriesberg, Geoff Johns
and all the other writers are really good

00:12:16.040 --> 00:12:18.000
at focusing on moments, not moves.

00:12:18.000 --> 00:12:22.470
Which is why the episodes are so much more
fun to watch.

00:12:22.470 --> 00:12:28.000
Which is why it almost doesn’t matter who
Harrison Wells ends up being, we’ll be so

00:12:28.000 --> 00:12:33.060
connected to the characters that it will be
all about the betrayal inside Team Flash not

00:12:33.060 --> 00:12:37.399
the Who part.

00:12:37.399 --> 00:12:38.730
On to big news,

00:12:38.730 --> 00:12:42.130
The producers said that when Barry meets the
reverse flash.

00:12:42.130 --> 00:12:46.780
He’ll be blurring his face, so Barry won’t
see who the Reverse Flash is and neither will

00:12:46.780 --> 00:12:47.780
we, the audience.

00:12:47.780 --> 00:12:49.680
They’re going to hold that card close to
the vest.

00:12:49.680 --> 00:12:57.940
Probably till the finale next year.

00:12:57.940 --> 00:13:01.880
Next week is the big two part crossover.

00:13:01.880 --> 00:13:04.120
If I have time I’ll do an extra bonus video
for it.

00:13:04.120 --> 00:13:05.500
Be sure to subscribe to get everything.

00:13:05.500 --> 00:13:08.630
It’s going to be an awesome two hour movie
on television.

00:13:08.630 --> 00:13:13.100
Think of it like TV Justice League.

00:13:13.100 --> 00:13:15.270
Quick reminder mobile links up here if you’re
on your phone or a tablet.

00:13:15.270 --> 00:13:16.839
Same as the links over here.

00:13:16.839 --> 00:13:17.839
Nice and simple.

00:13:17.839 --> 00:13:20.850
Click here to catch up on Arrow. and Click
here for last week’s Flash.

00:13:20.850 --> 00:13:21.850
Thanks for watching, see you guys tomorrow.

00:13:21.850 --> 00:13:21.920
High Fives!

